      "title": "Israeli tanks cross ‘yellow line’ boundary into Hamas-controlled central Gaza",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/18/israeli-tanks-cross-yellow-line-boundary-into-hamas-controlled-central-gaza",
      "description": "<p>First incursion across boundary since ceasefire deal comes as Eisenkot seeks to form government without Netanyahu</p><p>The Israeli military crossed into Hamas-controlled central Gaza on Wednesday in its first ground operation across the “yellow line” boundary since a fragile ceasefire was agreed last October, forcing dozens of displaced Palestinians to flee their tents.</p><p>Israeli tanks <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israeli-military-begins-new-thrust-gaza-kills-three-people-2026-11-18/\">rolled along the Salah al-Din road</a>, Gaza’s main north-south route, a day after the US-backed Board of Peace, a body overseeing the ceasefire, accused Israel and Hamas of failing to honour their commitments to end hostilities.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/18/israeli-tanks-cross-yellow-line-boundary-into-hamas-controlled-central-gaza\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
